 "rationale": "Step 2 radiation is mainly the third harmonic, k ~ 2-2.8. In 1D, gamma=2/width=12/cubic returns <= 4e-6 of the energy for k >= 1.5 and 1.9e-5 at k=1, while weak sponges that did better on the free-Gaussian check-4 test at L=50 (gamma=0.3: 0.127) return 13-20% at k >= 1.5. No design passed check 4 at L=50, so check 4 at L=50 could not decide between designs; the fast-radiation behaviour did. Width 12 (rather than 14) keeps a larger interior at a given L; the cubic ramp starts smoothly. Integrated damping per layer crossing gamma*width/4 = 6."
